# **Experiment 2: Implementation of Simple Two-Node Network**

### **Aim**

To establish and simulate a network connection between two nodes using Network Simulator-2 (NS2).

### ****

Save the file as `exp2.tcl`.

```

set ns [new Simulator]

$ns color 1 Blue
$ns color 2 Red

set nf [open out.nam w]
$ns namtrace-all $nf

set tf [open out.tr w]
$ns trace-all $tf

proc finish {} {
    global ns nf tf
    $ns flush-trace
    close $nf
    close $tf
    exec nam out.nam &
    exit 0
}

set n0 [$ns node]
set n1 [$ns node]

$n0 color red
$n1 color pink

$ns duplex-link $n0 $n1 2Mb 10ms DropTail

set udp [new Agent/UDP]
$ns attach-agent $n0 $udp

set null [new Agent/Null]
$ns attach-agent $n1 $null

$ns connect $udp $null

$udp set fid_ 2

set cbr [new Application/Traffic/CBR]
$cbr attach-agent $udp

$cbr set packetSize_ 500
$cbr set interval_ 0.01

$ns at 0.1 "$cbr start"
$ns at 0.5 "$cbr stop"
$ns at 5.0 "finish"

$ns run

```

### **Explanation**

| Statement         | Meaning                             |
| ----------------- | ----------------------------------- |
| `new Simulator`   | Creates NS2 simulator               |
| `node`            | Creates network nodes               |
| `duplex-link`     | Connects two nodes                  |
| `2Mb`             | Link bandwidth                      |
| `10ms`            | Link delay                          |
| `DropTail`        | Queue management technique          |
| `Agent/UDP`       | Creates UDP sender                  |
| `Agent/Null`      | Receives and discards packets       |
| `CBR`             | Generates constant bit-rate traffic |
| `packetSize_ 500` | Packet size is 500 bytes            |
| `interval_ 0.01`  | Packet generation interval          |
| `namtrace-all`    | Records NAM animation               |
| `trace-all`       | Records network events              |

### **Procedure**

**Step 1:** Open Ubuntu terminal.

**Step 2:** Create a Tcl file.

```
